{"type":"text","timestamp":1785400158114,"sessionID":"ses_04deff452ffeaoFMqgmoFc9cdM","part":{"id":"prt_fb22461630011JdQpeOdRjNpBf","messageID":"msg_fb2245cfa001ZANp2QlXHQcX7V","sessionID":"ses_04deff452ffeaoFMqgmoFc9cdM","type":"text","text":"Implemented core inventory API with real‑time updates and wired the frontend dashboard to consume it.\n\n**Backend (`backend/src/index.ts`)**\n- Added an in‑memory `inventory` array as a placeholder for PostgreSQL.\n- Implemented `GET /api/inventory` to return current inventory.\n- Implemented `POST /api/inventory` to add a vehicle, validate VIN, and broadcast the new entry via WebSocket.\n- Set up an HTTP server and a `WebSocketServer` (`ws`) for live push notifications.\n- Updated imports to include `WebSocketServer`.\n\n**Backend (`backend/package.json`)**\n- Added `ws` dependency for WebSocket support.\n\n**Frontend (`frontend/src/App.tsx`)**\n- Replaced static chart data with live data fetched from `/api/inventory`.\n- Added TypeScript interfaces for vehicle and chart data.\n- Implemented `useEffect` hooks to fetch inventory and establish a WebSocket connection for real‑time updates.\n- Dynamically computes vehicle “age” (current year − vehicle year) for the chart.\n\n**Frontend (`frontend/vite.config.ts`)**\n- Added Vite config with React plugin and proxy rules forwarding `/api` requests (including WebSocket upgrades) to the backend on `localhost:4000`.\n\n**Git**\n- Staged and committed all changes with a concise commit message.\n\nThe system now supports adding vehicles via POST, instantly pushes new entries to connected clients, and displays an up‑to‑date bar chart of vehicle ages on the dashboard.","time":{"start":1785400156515,"end":1785400158111}}}
